. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * The item plh0395i05: ``Schools and preschools should promote non-ge
> nder-typical activities that are not typical for children's gender'', emerges
>  as a strong proxy 
.         * for attitudes toward gender equality in the general population. Thi
> s item, clearly aligns with the core objective of challenging  gender stereot
> ypes and promoting an environment in 
.         * which individuals can realize their potential free from traditional
>  gender constraints. This rejection of normative assumptions based on gender,
>  actually  reflects a foundational principle 
.         * of gender equality. Moreover, this item captures a proactive stance
>  toward reshaping socialization processes and represents a progressive, preve
> ntive approach to addressing the root causes of gender inequality. 
.         * Accordingly, I run a linear OLS regression analysis with plh0395i05
>  as dependent variable and the dummy variable has_daughters interacted with t
> he male dummy as independent variable. The coefficient of interest 
.         *is the interacted term. Additionally, standard errors are clustered 
> at the hid (Current Wave Household Number) level, since it is possible that a
> ttitudes toward gender equality are correlated within the household 
.         * itself due to unobservable factors and/or common influences.
.         
.         reg plh0395i05 has_daughters has_kids male male_daughters age i.pgisc
> ed11 i.pgfamstd i.corigin i.eintritt, cluster(hid)

